<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Monitor user sessions in RUM on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/4-rum/</link><description>Recent content in Monitor user sessions in RUM on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/4-rum/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>User Sessions</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/4-rum/1-rum-sessions/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/4-rum/1-rum-sessions/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;In Splunk RUM, a &lt;strong&gt;session&lt;/strong&gt; is a continuous period of user activity on your app (up to four hours, ending after inactivity or when the app closes). RUM sessions inform analyses like funnels and feature adoption timeseries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Session details&lt;/strong&gt; show metadata, replay events, and a waterfall of spans (loads, requests, custom events, web vitals, errors). See &lt;a href="https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-observability-cloud/digital-experience-monitoring/real-user-monitoring/key-concepts-in-splunk-rum" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Key concepts in Splunk RUM&lt;svg class="link-ext" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="M7 17 17 7"/&gt;&lt;path d="M9 7h8v8"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
 for more info.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>RUM Application Overview</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/4-rum/4-rum-app-view/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/4-rum/4-rum-app-view/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;At the top of the session page, click the breadcrumb link to the workshop app.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;section class="exercise"&gt;
&lt;header class="exercise__bar"&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-label"&gt;Exercise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-divider" aria-hidden="true"&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-title"&gt;Find critical workflows&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__body"&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will now see a dashboard breaking down RUM metrics by &lt;strong&gt;User Experience&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Front-end Health&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Back-end Health&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Custom Workflows&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Pages&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Network Requests&lt;/strong&gt;, and a &lt;strong&gt;Map View&lt;/strong&gt;. Current metrics are compared to historic metrics (1 hour by default).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="../images/rum-metric-map-charts.png" alt="RUM Dashboard" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click through each of the tabs and examine the data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs" data-tabs&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs__list" role="tablist"&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-4-rum-4-rum-app-view-md-1-1--0-tab-0" class="tabs__btn is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-4-rum-4-rum-app-view-md-1-1--0-panel-0" tabindex="0" data-tab-label="Questions"&gt;Questions&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-4-rum-4-rum-app-view-md-1-1--0-tab-1" class="tabs__btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-4-rum-4-rum-app-view-md-1-1--0-panel-1" tabindex="-1" data-tab-label="Answers"&gt;Answers&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-4-rum-4-rum-app-view-md-1-1--0-panel-0" class="tabs__panel is-active" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-4-rum-4-rum-app-view-md-1-1--0-tab-0" data-tab-label="Questions"&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you examine the charts in the &lt;strong&gt;Custom Workflows&lt;/strong&gt; tab, what chart shows the &lt;strong&gt;latency&lt;/strong&gt; for &lt;code&gt;PlaceOrder&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the &lt;strong&gt;Map View&lt;/strong&gt; tab, where is the largest request volume coming from?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-4-rum-4-rum-app-view-md-1-1--0-panel-1" class="tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-4-rum-4-rum-app-view-md-1-1--0-tab-1" hidden data-tab-label="Answers"&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom Event Latency P75&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure you are on the &lt;strong&gt;Custom Workflows&lt;/strong&gt; tab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To identify problematic user sessions, we will use the latency spikes in the &lt;strong&gt;Custom Event Latency&lt;/strong&gt; chart.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the &lt;strong&gt;Custom Workflow Latency&lt;/strong&gt; chart click on the &lt;strong&gt;see all&lt;/strong&gt; link under the chart title.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="../images/rum-see-all.png" alt="RUM See All Custom Workflows" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Tag Spotlight</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/4-rum/5-tag-spotlight/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/4-rum/5-tag-spotlight/</guid><description>&lt;section class="exercise"&gt;
&lt;header class="exercise__bar"&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-label"&gt;Exercise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-divider" aria-hidden="true"&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-title"&gt;Filter to slow PlaceOrder sessions&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__body"&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This dashboard displays all tags associated with the RUM data, key-value pairs automatically generated by the RUM instrumentation. Tags are used to filter data and build charts and tables. The Tag Spotlight view lets you drill down into individual user sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="../images/rum-tag-spotlight.png" alt="RUM Tag Spotlight" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change the timeframe to &lt;strong&gt;Last 1 hour&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;(1)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;!--* Click **Add Filters**, select **OS Version**, click **!=** and select **Synthetics** and **RUM.LoadGen** then click the &lt;button class="btn-inline btn-inline--filled" type="button" style="--btn-color: #1d5d99"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Apply Filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt; button **(2)**.--&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find the &lt;strong&gt;Operation&lt;/strong&gt; chart, locate &lt;strong&gt;PlaceOrder&lt;/strong&gt; in the list, click on it and select &lt;strong&gt;Add to filter&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;(2)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>